    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract shard-node admission and accounting policy. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>All shard-count enforcement in ThemisDB routes through this interface so that edition limits, signed plugin upgrades, and operational caps share a single, auditable enforcement surface.</para>
<para>Hierarchy overview: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_i_shard_limit_policy_1af6022d52adcd799748bb57b8c889c537" kindref="member">IShardLimitPolicy</ref><sp/><sp/><sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">this</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>file)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">└──<sp/>EditionManager::installShardPolicy()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>└──<sp/>EditionManager::checkNodeLimit()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>└──<sp/>ShardingManager<sp/>—<sp/>enforces<sp/>on<sp/>shard<sp/>join</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Thread safety: all implementations must be individually thread-safe.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>A policy&apos;s <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_i_shard_limit_policy_1a2eae8a65e8dc419ab2c7e2ac72523498" kindref="member">maxNodes()</ref> must never exceed the compile-time edition constant <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1edition_1a6c6823dc5c27228bbb08357e9819a263" kindref="member">edition::SHARDING_MAX_NODES</ref> (enforced by EditionManager::installShardPolicy before accepting the policy). On Hyperscaler binaries (SHARDING_MAX_NODES == -1) the ceiling is unlimited and any positive <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_i_shard_limit_policy_1a2eae8a65e8dc419ab2c7e2ac72523498" kindref="member">maxNodes()</ref> value is accepted. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
